This paper establishes the existence of nontrivial weak solutions for a specific class of quasilinear elliptic systems with convective terms and $p$-Laplacian, given by the equations: 
\begin{equation*}
\left\{\begin{array}{ll}
-\Delta_{p}u+a(x)|u|^{p-2}u+b(x)|u|^{p-2}v=\lambda u^{q-1},\quad x\in\mathbb{R}^{N},\\
-\Delta_{p}v+a(x)|v|^{p-2}v+b(x)|u|^{p-2}v=\lambda v^{m-1},\quad x\in\mathbb{R}^{N},
\end{array}
\right.
\end{equation*}
where $\lambda$ is a positive constant, $p$ and $q$ are positive real numbers, and $a$ and $b$ are functions in the Sobolev space $L^{2s}(\mathbb{R}^{N})$. The existence of these solutions is proven using the mountain pass theorem and the Nehari manifold.
